ion or monitoring\", \"ev\": [{\"loc\": \"summary\", \"q\": \"AFP surveillance and stool specimen timeliness at the national and provincial levels have met performance targets\"}]}], \"methods_quotes\": [{\"loc\": \"note\", \"q\": \"Adequate stool specimen is defined as two stool specimens collected ≥24 hours apart, both within 14 days of paralysis onset\"}, {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"Vaccination histories, based on parental recall and vaccination cards\"}, {\"loc\": \"note\", \"q\": \"WHO operational targets for countries with endemic-poliovirus transmission are NPAFP detection rates of ≥2 cases per 100,000 population aged <15 years\"}, {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"periodic testing of sewage samples for polioviruses\"}], \"confidence\": \"high\", \"uncertain_fields\": []}", "type": "text"}]}